high school, associate, bachelor, master, doctorate).\n","*   Y-axis → Number of applicants.\n","*   Bars (grouped by loan intent) → Each education level has multiple bars showing how many applicants applied for different loan purposes (personal, education, medical, venture, home improvement, debt consolidation).\n","\n","Bachelor degree holders dominate overall applications, spread across multiple loan intents (especially personal,medical and debt consolidation).\n","\n","High school graduates tend to apply more for personal loans, with fewer applications in categories like venture or home improvement.\n","\n","Master’s and Doctorate holders are smaller applicant groups, but they show noticeable interest in education loans and home improvement loans.\n","\n","Associate degree holders show Moderate participation, mostly in personal and debt consolidation loans."],"metadata":{"id":"crM8yHiOeigB"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Box plot\n","sns.boxplot(x=\"person_home_ownership\", y=\"loan_amnt\", data=df)\n","plt.title(\"Loan amount vs person_home_ownership\")\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"id":"Lca1BWEhX6XX","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":472},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1778428837623,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":527,"user":{"displayName":"Kannamma Mohan","userId":"15930429332604887931"}},"outputId":"3751c0c2-19c6-4da1-a1a9-538ac3a1c77b"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":[" This categorical box plot is comparing loan amounts (loan_amnt) across different home ownership statuses (person_home_ownership).\n","*   X-axis → Home ownership categories: rent, own, mortgage, other.\n","*   Y-axis → Loan amount requested (ranging up to ~35,000).\n","*   Boxes → Show the distribution of loan amounts for each category (median, quartiles, and spread).\n","*   Dots above boxes → Outliers (individual applicants requesting unusually high loan amounts compared to the rest of their group).\n","\n","Renters: Loan amounts are spread out, with a moderate median. Some outliers request very high loans.\n","\n","Owners: Tend to request smaller loans compared to mortgage holders, with fewer extreme outliers.\n","\n","Mortgage holders: Show higher loan amounts overall, with a higher median and wider spread. This makes sense — people with mortgages often request larger loans (home improvement, debt consolidation).\n","\n","Other: This category is small, with a narrow distribution, suggesting fewer applicants.\n"],"metadata":{"id":"mKn5CcTResYX"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Numerical variables\n","num_cols = ['cb_person_cred_hist_length','credit_score']\n","\n","for col in num_cols:\n","    plt.figure(figsize=(10,4))\n","    plt.subplot(1,2,1)\n","    sns.histplot(df[col], kde=True, bins=30)\n","    plt.title(f\"Histogram of {col}\")\n","\n","    plt.subplot(1,2,2)\n","    sns.boxplot(x=df[col])\n","    plt.title(f\"Boxplot of {col}\")\n","    plt.show()\n","\n"],"metadata":{"id":"a4eu2JbhX6Fo","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":770},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1778428844922,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":1271,"user":{"displayName":"Kannamma Mohan","userId":"15930429332604887931"}},"outputId":"f365422b-0e40-4444-f15b-e17ce4c097cd"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1000x400 with 2 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1000x400 with 2 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["**Histogram of cb_person_cred_hist_length**\n","Shows how many applicants fall into different ranges of credit history length.\n","Right-skewed: Most applicants have short credit histories (0–10 years).\n","Very few have long histories beyond 20 years.\n","\n","**Box plot of cb_person_cred_hist_length**\n","The box is narrow, meaning most applicants cluster around short histories.\n","Outliers extend far to the right, representing a small number of applicants with unusually long credit histories."],"metadata":{"id":"M7V_F0SXmuai"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["**Histogram of credit_score**\n","Roughly bell-shaped distribution.\n","Most applicants have mid-range credit scores, with fewer at the very low or very high ends.\n","This suggests the dataset is centered around average credit scores."],"metadata":{"id":"SX07QxbSni0m"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["**Boxplot of credit_score**\n","Shows the spread of credit scores.\n","The central box captures the middle 50% of applicants.\n","Outliers exist on both ends, meaning some applicants have exceptionally low or high scores compared to the majority."],"metadata":{"id":"Q5gLaJ1onzes"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["### **Bivariate Analysis**"],"metadata":{"id":"XG8K7QQrjAGk"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Barplot of Credit History Length vs Loan Status\n","sns.barplot(x='loan_status', y='cb_person_cred_hist_length', data=df)\n","plt.title(\"Credit History Length vs Loan Status\")\n","plt.xticks([0,1], ['Rejected (0)', 'Approved (1)'])\n","plt.ylabel(\"Credit History Length (years)\")\n","plt.show()\n"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":472},"id":"C3sgnzWcSRO6","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1778428851181,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":874,"user":{"displayName":"Kannamma Mohan","userId":"15930429332604887931"}},"outputId":"2df30b20-d630-4ae6-eaac-3e033fceac71"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["The above bar chart is comparing average credit history length (in years) between applicants whose loans were rejected (0) and those whose loans were approved (1).\n","*   X-axis → Loan status (Rejected vs Approved).\n","*  Y-axis → Average credit history length in years.\n","Both bars are nearly the same height.\n","Applicants who were approved and those who were rejected have similar average credit history lengths.\n","This suggests that credit history length alone is not a decisive factor in loan approval decisions in this dataset.\n"],"metadata":{"id":"MBBuxohEj71l"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Calculating approval rate by credit history length\n","approval_rate = df.groupby('cb_person_cred_hist_length')['loan_status'].mean().reset_index()\n","\n","# Line chart\n","sns.lineplot(x='cb_person_cred_hist_length', y='loan_status', data=approval_rate, marker='o')\n","plt.title(\"Loan Approval Rate vs Credit History Length\")\n","plt.xlabel(\"Credit History Length (years)\")\n","plt.ylabel(\"Approval Rate\")\n","plt.show()\n"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":472},"id":"iuyGnTeATgrP","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1778428856999,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":238,"user":{"displayName":"Kannamma Mohan","userId":"15930429332604887931"}},"outputId":"07f98b81-1227-4ff5-fef9-26054cf923c1"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["The above line chart is showing the loan approval rate as a function of credit history length (in years).\n","\n","\n","*   X-axis → Credit history length (0–30 years).\n","*   Y-axis → Approval rate (proportion of applicants approved).\n","The plotted line shows how approval rates change as credit history length increases.\n","For shorter credit histories (0–10 years), approval rates are relatively low and stable.\n","\n","Between 10–20 years, approval rates fluctuate but remain modest.\n","\n","After 20 years, approval rates rise noticeably and show more variability, suggesting that very long credit histories improve approval chances.\n","\n","The overall trend indicates that longer credit histories are associated with higher approval rates, though not perfectly linear.\n","\n"],"metadata":{"id":"K0xYJI42lhhJ"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Scatterplot\n","sns.scatterplot(x='credit_score', y='loan_int_rate', data=df)\n","plt.title(\"Credit Score vs Loan Interest Rate\")\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":472},"id":"c9nUG5l5gTAu","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1778428865997,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":1276,"user":{"displayName":"Kannamma Mohan","userId":"15930429332604887931"}},"outputId":"a0621481-edf0-4c52-d6de-945dbd70898d"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["This scatter plot is showing the relationship between credit score and loan interest rate.\n","*  X-axis → Credit score (roughly 400–850).\n","*  Y-axis → Loan interest rate (roughly 6–20%).\n","Each point represents an applicant’s credit score and the interest rate they were offered.\n","\n","Applicants with higher credit scores tend to receive lower interest rates.\n","Applicants with lower credit scores face higher interest rates.\n","The scatter shows a downward trend, which aligns with lending practices — better creditworthiness reduces risk, so lenders reward it with cheaper loans.\n","Some variability exists - not every applicant with the same score gets the exact same rate, but the overall pattern holds."],"metadata":{"id":"7KRAGIlrqPGR"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["sns.scatterplot(x='loan_amnt', y='loan_percent_income', data=df)\n","plt.title(\"loan amount vs loan percent income\")\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":472},"id":"w9AHB72au_0U","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1778428872429,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":618,"user":{"displayName":"Kannamma Mohan","userId":"15930429332604887931"}},"outputId":"835accd2-3352-405a-ceb3-1a300761cc5f"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["This scatter plot is showing the relationship between loan amount (loan_amnt) and loan percent income (loan_percent_income).\n","*  X-axis → Loan amount requested (up to ~25,000).\n","*  Y-axis → Loan percent income (the fraction of income the loan represents, mostly between 0.0 and 0.6).\n","Each point represents an applicant’s loan request relative to their income.\n","Most data points are clustered in the lower ranges of both variables.\n","Most applicants request loans under 25,000, and those loans typically represent less than 60% of their income.\n","\n","Risk perspective: Applicants whose loan percent income is higher (closer to 0.6) are riskier, since the loan consumes a large share of their income.\n","\n","Loan size vs affordability: Larger loan amounts don’t always mean higher percent income — some applicants with high incomes can afford larger loans without crossing into risky ratios.\n","\n","Outliers: A few points may represent applicants with unusually high loan percent income, indicating loans that are disproportionately large compared to their income."],"metadata":{"id":"VlBA9vlmrrXe"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# loan_intent vs loan_amount\n","sns.barplot(x='loan_intent', y='loan_amnt', data=df, estimator=sum)\n","plt.title(\"loan_intent vs loan_amount\")\n","plt.xticks(rotation=45)\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":561},"id":"YqkLm86kgSsZ","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1778428882579,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":5238,"user":{"displayName":"Kannamma Mohan","userId":"15930429332604887931"}},"outputId":"ce5ca62d-007e-4759-98ff-42bacd23ae36"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["The above bar plot is comparing loan intent categories against the total loan amounts requested.\n","*   X-axis → Loan intent (personal, education, medical, venture, home improvement, debt consolidation).\n","*  Y-axis → Total loan amount (sum of all loans requested under each intent).\n","\n","Each bar shows the aggregate loan size for that particular purpose.\n","Education loan secures the top position and medical loan follows.\n","The total amount for home improvement is the least."],"metadata":{"id":"x6_Jd_RFrH_o"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["#Loan defaults vs Loan status\n","ct = pd.crosstab(df['previous_loan_defaults_on_file'], df['loan_status_category'], normalize='index')\n","sns.heatmap(ct, annot=True, cmap=\"Blues\")\n","plt.title(\" Loan defaults vs Loan status\")\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":472},"id":"XOdZYw5_xmVX","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1778428896995,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":292,"user":{"displayName":"Kannamma Mohan","userId":"15930429332604887931"}},"outputId":"d84b2e92-cb83-42e8-c777-c851507e637b"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 640x480 with 2 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["This heatmap is comparing previous loan defaults on file against loan status outcomes.\n","*   X-axis → Loan status (approved vs rejected).\n","*   Y-axis → Default history (yes or no).\n","Values inside cells → Normalized proportions (each row adds up to 1).\n","\n","Color intensity → Higher values are darker blue.\n","\n","**No defaults**:\n","\n","45% approved\n","\n","55% rejected\n","Applicants without defaults have a fair chance of approval, though rejection is still slightly more common.\n","\n","**Yes defaults:**\n","\n","0% approved\n","\n","100% rejected\n","\n"," Applicants with defaults are always rejected in this dataset.\n","\n","This makes it visually clear that default history is a **decisive factor** in loan approval decisions.\n","\n","\n"],"metadata":{"id":"IBq6blOZvI3f"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Cross-tabulation of credit score category and previous defaults vs loan status\n","ct = pd.crosstab(\n","    [df['credit_score_category'], df['previous_loan_defaults_on_file']],\n","    df['loan_status_category'],\n","    normalize='index'\n",")\n","\n","# Heatmap\n","plt.figure(figsize=(10,6))\n","sns.heatmap(ct, annot=True, cmap=\"Blues\")\n","plt.title(\"(Credit Score Category + Previous Defaults) vs Loan Status\")\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":544},"id":"zWK2isJe0POM","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1778428911813,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":344,"user":{"displayName":"Kannamma Mohan","userId":"15930429332604887931"}},"outputId":"ece90882-a351-4d15-cc88-077f08a6a096"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1000x600 with 2 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["This heatmap is showing how credit score category combined with previous default history influences loan status outcomes.\n","\n","*   Columns (X-axis) → Loan status (0 = rejected, 1 = approved).\n","*   Rows (Y-axis) → Each combination of credit score category + default status (e.g., good-no, good-yes).\n","\n","Cell values → Proportion of applicants in that group who were rejected vs approved.\n","\n","Color intensity → Darker blue = higher proportion.\n","\n","**Defaults present (“yes”):**\n","\n","Across all categories (low, fair, average, good, excellent), applicants with defaults are always rejected (100%).\n","\n","This confirms defaults are a **decisive factor **overriding credit score.\n","\n","**No defaults (“no”):**\n","\n","**Excellent-no** → 70% approved, 30% rejected → highest approval rate.\n","\n","**Good-no** → 67% approved, 33% rejected → strong approval rate, but slightly lower than excellent.\n","\n","**Average-no** → 61% approved, 39% rejected → moderate approval rate.\n","\n","**Fair-no** → 50% approved, 50% rejected → balanced outcome.\n","\n","**Low-no** → Only 23% approved, 77% rejected → lowest approval rate among those without defaults.\n"],"metadata":{"id":"r7ACBjADxfmS"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Selecting the raw numerical features\n","corr = df[['loan_amnt','loan_int_rate','person_income']].corr()\n","\n","# Plotting heatmap\n","plt.figure(figsize=(6,4))\n","sns.heatmap(corr, annot=True, cmap=\"Blues\", center=0)\n","plt.title(\"Correlation Heatmap of Loan Amount, Interest Rate, and Income\")\n","plt.show()\n"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":391},"id":"kSlYCiFNAieW","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1778428919411,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":188,"user":{"displayName":"Kannamma Mohan","userId":"15930429332604887931"}},"outputId":"66461352-de95-4f92-ed81-0122a2349906"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 600x400 with 2 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["The above heatmap is showing the correlation among three numerical features: loan amount, loan interest rate, and applicant income.\n","\n","Loan amount vs income → Correlation = 0.24 (moderate positive). Applicants with higher incomes tend to request larger loans.\n","\n","Loan amount vs interest rate → Correlation = 0.15 (weak positive). Slight tendency for larger loans to have higher interest rates, but the relationship is weak.\n","\n","Income vs interest rate → Correlation = 0.0015 (essentially zero). Applicant income has almost no direct correlation with the interest rate offered.\n","\n","Income matters for loan size: Higher earners request bigger loans, which is intuitive.\n","\n","Interest rate is not income-driven: Lenders don’t directly tie interest rates to income; instead, they likely rely on credit score, default history, or loan intent.\n","\n","Loan size vs interest rate: The weak positive correlation suggests that loan size alone doesn’t strongly influence the rate — other risk factors dominate."],"metadata":{"id":"84T_IkXKz0J_"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["### **Multivariate Analysis**"],"metadata":{"id":"Kw1CoFK6DC3Q"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["pivot = pd.pivot_table(df,\n","                       values='loan_status',\n","                       index=['credit_score_category'],\n","                       columns=['person_education'],\n","                       aggfunc='mean')\n","\n","sns.heatmap(pivot, annot=True, cmap=\"Blues\")\n","plt.title(\"Approval Rate by Credit Score & Education\")\n","plt.show()\n"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":472},"id":"a62Hl6OLCmLX","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1778428926132,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":252,"user":{"displayName":"Kannamma Mohan","userId":"15930429332604887931"}},"outputId":"ec135f52-319f-47fc-8532-3ccc67dbaa6b"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 640x480 with 2 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["The above heatmap is showing loan approval rates across combinations of credit score category and education level.\n","\n","*   X-axis → Education levels (associate, bachelor, doctorate, high school, master).\n","*   Y-axis → Credit score categories (low, fair, average, good, excellent).\n","\n","Cell values → Approval rate (proportion of applicants approved).\n","\n","Color intensity → Darker blue = higher approval rate.\n","\n","**Excellent scores:**\n","\n","Highest approval rate (0.50) for bachelor’s degree holders.\n","\n","Much lower approval for associate and doctorate levels (0.0–0.2), showing education modifies the effect of score.\n","\n","**Good scores:**\n","\n","Approval rates are consistently moderate (~0.20–0.24) across education levels.\n","\n","This confirms that “good” scores underperform compared to “excellent.”\n","\n","**Average & Fair scores:**\n","\n","Stable approval rates (~0.21–0.25) across all education levels.\n","\n","Education doesn’t strongly shift outcomes here.\n","\n","**Low scores: **\n","\n","Generally low approval (~0.22–0.24), but doctorate holders with low scores show a spike (0.36), which is unusual.\n","\n","This suggests lenders may weigh advanced education as a compensating factor."],"metadata":{"id":"VtymNBII0yuT"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["**Loan Status Analysis - DashBoard**"],"metadata":{"id":"56ARGjhYWySD"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["![Screenshot 2026-05-17 060154.png](data:image/png;base64,)"],"metadata":{"id":"fiz3MpraWcvI"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["![Screenshot 2026-05-17 060902.png](data:image/png;base64,)"],"metadata":{"id":"XsWhechYZQXe"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["PowerBI dashboard pdf:\n","\n","https://drive.google.com/file/d/1RSID0DafmRHJqFGpTwd8rY-gHqgd9_zn/view?usp=sharing\n","\n","PowerBI dashboard file:\n","\n","https://drive.google.com/file/d/1AEKc8Xub_wuYGjNE1WotUBtuRvuZUGcZ/view?usp=drive_link\n","\n","Loan Status analysis insights:\n","\n","https://drive.google.com/file/d/1G6yD3VWay-Yui1jR344nbdwADr2P22hC/view?usp=drive_link\n","\n","\n","All files:\n","\n","https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1GuLeSYGvrx6VZ0OFvQnYttBf02-BqCxN?usp=sharing"],"metadata":{"id":"HsHmX281OuQX"}}]}